            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for to presume, then the Portuguese for plausible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a condição",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a condição — \"the condition\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Vou contigo, com uma condição: voltamos cedo. I will go with you on one condition: we come back early."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Com a condição de + infinitive. Condições de trabalho — working conditions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "condição is a learned borrowing from Latin condiciō \"an agreement, a condition\" (EtymDB, Lewis & Short), often spelt conditiō in later Latin, built on condīcere \"to talk together, to agree on\", from dīcere \"to say\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
