        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: desde que",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "desde que — \"provided that, as long as; since (in time)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Podes ir à festa desde que voltes antes da meia-noite. You can go to the party as long as you come back before midnight."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With the subjunctive it sets a condition: desde que voltes. With the indicative it means since: desde que cheguei."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "desde que is built from desde \"since\", usually traced to Latin dē + ex + dē, all meaning \"from\" (Lewis & Short), and que."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
